,"html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101141#issuecomment-3065730808","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101141","id":3065730808,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62u1b4","user":{"login":"BlueCube3310","id":53150244,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTUwMjQ0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53150244?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310","html_url":"https://github.com/BlueCube3310","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-12T15:54:28Z","updated_at":"2025-07-12T15:54:28Z","body":"> By the way, does this technique also apply to SH evaluation for lightmap dynamic probes? I'm wondering if this can help resolve #108526. I've tried to `max()` each component of the ambient light to `0.0` but it didn't help improve visuals (although it did get rid of negative pixels in the final image).\r\n\r\nDynamic probes make use of L2 spherical harmonics, while the Geomerics method only applies to L1. There has been some research in terms of de-ringing/windowing L2 SH, but it generally doesn't look as good as a non-linear model: https://www.activision.com/cdn/research/Deringing_Spherical_Harmonics_PPS_V2.pdf","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3065730808/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3065915112","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101141#issuecomment-3065915112","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101141","id":3065915112,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62vibo","user":{"login":"BlueCube3310","id":53150244,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTUwMjQ0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53150244?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310","html_url":"https://github.com/BlueCube3310","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-12T17:57:46Z","updated_at":"2025-07-12T17:57:46Z","body":"I pushed a fix for the NaNs, the light's contrast should also look slightly better.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3065915112/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]